{"name":"Environmental","hex":"#b1b5a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"environmental","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the environment.","Environmentally friendly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any factor relating to the physical environment in which hardware is operated, such as the room temperature or the number of racks used to hold equipment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/environmental"}],"entries":[{"title":"Natural environment","blocks":[{"text":"The natural environment or natural world encompasses all biotic and abiotic things occurring naturally, meaning in this case not artificial. The term is most often applied to Earth or some parts of Earth. This environment encompasses the interaction of all living species, climate, weather and natural resources that affect human survival and economic activity. The concept of the natural environment can be distinguished as components:"},{"items":["Complete ecological units that function as natural systems without massive civilized human intervention, including all vegetation, microorganisms, soil, rocks, plateaus, mountains, the atmosphere and natural phenomena that occur within their boundaries and their nature.","Universal natural resources and physical phenomena that lack clear-cut boundaries, such as air, water and climate, as well as energy, radiation, electric charge and magnetism, not originating from civilized human actions."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Hopetoun_falls.jpg/330px-Hopetoun_falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_environment","wikidata":"Q43619"},{"title":"Ecology","blocks":[{"text":"Ecology is the natural science which studies the interactions between organisms and their environments. Ecology considers organisms at the community, ecosystem, and biosphere levels. Ecology overlaps with the sciences of biogeography, evolutionary biology, genetics, and ethology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Bufo_boreas.jpg/330px-Bufo_boreas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecology","wikidata":"Q7150"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Sahara_satellite_hires.jpg/500px-Sahara_satellite_hires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Sahara_satellite_hires.jpg/1280px-Sahara_satellite_hires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Sahara_satellite_hires.jpg/500px-Sahara_satellite_hires.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An image of the Sahara Desert from satellite. It is the world's largest hot desert and third-largest desert after the polar deserts.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASahara_satellite_hires.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Blue_Linckia_Starfish.JPG/500px-Blue_Linckia_Starfish.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Blue_Linckia_Starfish.JPG/500px-Blue_Linckia_Starfish.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coral reefs have significant marine biodiversity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Linckia_Starfish.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hawaii_Creek.jpg/500px-Hawaii_Creek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hawaii_Creek.jpg/1280px-Hawaii_Creek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x",